Usage: head [OPTION]... [FILE]...

Print the first 10 lines of each FILE to standard output.
With more than one FILE, precede each with a header giving the file name.

With no FILE, or when FILE is -, read standard input.

OPTIONS:
  -c, --bytes ARG        print the first NUM bytes of each file; with the
                         leading '-',
                         print all but the last NUM bytes
  -n, --lines ARG        print the first NUM lines instead of the first 10; with
                         the
                         leading '-', print all but the last NUM lines
  -q, --quiet            never print headers giving file names for multiple
                         files
      --silent           never print headers giving file names for multiple
                         files
  -v, --verbose          always print headers giving file names for multiple
                         files
  -z, --zero-terminated  line delimiter is NUL, not newline
      --help             display this help and exit
  -V, --version          output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
